{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdRfEKywWmww5h7aeLX6iq","type":"tool_result","content":"70\tThat is, if each `(u i, v i)` belongs to the kernel, then so does the pair `((f ^ 𝑨) u , (f ^ 𝑨) v)`.\n71\t\n72\t```agda\n73\t  HomKerComp : 𝑨 ∣≈ kerRel _≈_ h\n74\t  HomKerComp f {u}{v} kuv = Goal\n75\t    where\n76\t    fhuv : (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ u) ≈ (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ v)\n77\t    fhuv = cong Interp (refl , kuv)\n78\t\n79\t    lem1 : h ((f ^ 𝑨) u) ≈ (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ u)\n80\t    lem1 = IsHom.compatible hhom\n81\t\n82\t    lem2 : (f ^ 𝑩) (h ∘ v) ≈ h ((f ^ 𝑨) v)\n83\t    lem2 = sym (IsHom.compatible hhom)\n84\t\n85\t    Goal : h ((f ^ 𝑨) u) ≈ h ((f ^ 𝑨) v)\n86\t    Goal = trans lem1 (trans fhuv lem2)\n87\t```\n88\t\n89\tThe kernel of a homomorphism is a congruence of the domain, which we construct as follows.\n90\t\n91\t```agda\n92\t  kercon : Con 𝑨 ρᵇ\n93\t  kercon =  kerRel _≈_ h ,\n94\t            mkcon (λ x → cong hmap x)(kerRelOfEquiv isEquivalence h)(HomKerComp)\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\tNow that we have a congruence, we can construct the quotient relative to the kernel.\n98\t\n99\t```agda\n100\t  kerquo : Algebra α ρᵇ\n101\t  kerquo = 𝑨 ╱ kercon\n102\t\n103\tker[_⇒_]_ :  {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} (𝑨 : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ) (𝑩 : Algebra β ρᵇ) → hom 𝑨 𝑩 → Algebra _ _\n104\tker[ 𝑨 ⇒ 𝑩 ] h = kerquo h\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\t\n108\t#### The canonical projection\n109\t\n110\tGiven an algebra `𝑨` and a congruence `θ`, the *canonical projection* is a map\n111\tfrom `𝑨` onto `𝑨 ╱ θ` that is constructed, and proved epimorphic, as follows.\n112\t\n113\t```agda\n114\tmodule _ {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} {𝑨 : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ}{𝑩 : Algebra β ρᵇ} (h : hom 𝑨 𝑩) where\n115\t  open IsCongruence\n116\t\n117\t  πepi : (θ : Con 𝑨 ℓ) → epi 𝑨 (𝑨 ╱ θ)\n118\t  πepi θ = p , pepi\n119\t    where\n120\t\n121\t    open Setoid 𝔻[ 𝑨 ╱ θ ]    using () renaming ( sym to ≈sym ; refl to ≈refl )\n122\t    open IsHom {𝑨 = (𝑨 ╱ θ)}  using ( compatible )\n123\t    open IsEpi\n124\t\n125\t    p : 𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑨 ╱ θ ]\n126\t    p ⟨$⟩ x = x\n127\t    p .cong = reflexive (θ .proj₂)\n128\t\n129\t    pepi : IsEpi 𝑨 (𝑨 ╱ θ) p"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e309476-c72e-40a3-be6c-85cba8abe6e7","uuid":"bd0f3636-007c-419a-92cb-8adb56e2c370","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:47:55.672Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Setoid/Homomorphisms/Kernels.lagda.md","content":"That is, if each `(u i, v i)` belongs to the kernel, then so does the pair `((f ^ 𝑨) u , (f ^ 𝑨) v)`.\n\n```agda\n  HomKerComp : 𝑨 ∣≈ kerRel _≈_ h\n  HomKerComp f {u}{v} kuv = Goal\n    where\n    fhuv : (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ u) ≈ (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ v)\n    fhuv = cong Interp (refl , kuv)\n\n    lem1 : h ((f ^ 𝑨) u) ≈ (f ^ 𝑩)(h ∘ u)\n    lem1 = IsHom.compatible hhom\n\n    lem2 : (f ^ 𝑩) (h ∘ v) ≈ h ((f ^ 𝑨) v)\n    lem2 = sym (IsHom.compatible hhom)\n\n    Goal : h ((f ^ 𝑨) u) ≈ h ((f ^ 𝑨) v)\n    Goal = trans lem1 (trans fhuv lem2)\n```\n\nThe kernel of a homomorphism is a congruence of the domain, which we construct as follows.\n\n```agda\n  kercon : Con 𝑨 ρᵇ\n  kercon =  kerRel _≈_ h ,\n            mkcon (λ x → cong hmap x)(kerRelOfEquiv isEquivalence h)(HomKerComp)\n```\n\nNow that we have a congruence, we can construct the quotient relative to the kernel.\n\n```agda\n  kerquo : Algebra α ρᵇ\n  kerquo = 𝑨 ╱ kercon\n\nker[_⇒_]_ :  {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} (𝑨 : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ) (𝑩 : Algebra β ρᵇ) → hom 𝑨 𝑩 → Algebra _ _\nker[ 𝑨 ⇒ 𝑩 ] h = kerquo h\n```\n\n\n#### The canonical projection\n\nGiven an algebra `𝑨` and a congruence `θ`, the *canonical projection* is a map\nfrom `𝑨` onto `𝑨 ╱ θ` that is constructed, and proved epimorphic, as follows.\n\n```agda\nmodule _ {𝑆 : Signature 𝓞 𝓥} {𝑨 : Algebra {𝑆 = 𝑆} α ρᵃ}{𝑩 : Algebra β ρᵇ} (h : hom 𝑨 𝑩) where\n  open IsCongruence\n\n  πepi : (θ : Con 𝑨 ℓ) → epi 𝑨 (𝑨 ╱ θ)\n  πepi θ = p , pepi\n    where\n\n    open Setoid 𝔻[ 𝑨 ╱ θ ]    using () renaming ( sym to ≈sym ; refl to ≈refl )\n    open IsHom {𝑨 = (𝑨 ╱ θ)}  using ( compatible )\n    open IsEpi\n\n    p : 𝔻[ 𝑨 ] ⟶ 𝔻[ 𝑨 ╱ θ ]\n    p ⟨$⟩ x = x\n    p .cong = reflexive (θ .proj₂)\n\n    pepi : IsEpi 𝑨 (𝑨 ╱ θ) p","numLines":60,"startLine":70,"totalLines":163}}}
